# Pre-push & Lovable / Supabase sync

Before you **finish a task**, **suggest pushing**, or **confirm a branch is ready to merge**, treat [docs/ops/deployment-sync-guide.md](docs/ops/deployment-sync-guide.md) as the canonical checklist. Summarize or run the relevant steps; do not skip them for "small" changes if they touch migrations, edge functions, Supabase types, or production behavior.

## Minimum commands (when code changed)

Run and address failures before push:

- `npm run test`
- `npm run build`
- `npm run lint` on touched files (whole-repo lint has known noise)
- `npm run check:edge` when Deno is available (edge TS changes)
- `npm run check:edge-logging` when adding or editing edge function HTTP entrypoints (`supabase/functions/*/index.ts`)
- `npm run check:edge-coverage-manifest` when adding/removing `supabase/functions/*` or editing `[functions.*]` / `EdgeCoverage.tsx`
- `npm run check:prepush` when `bash` is available (Git Bash / WSL / Unix) for the full scripted gate before a high-stakes push

## Always remember

| What | Effect on sync |
|------|----------------|
| `supabase/migrations/` | Applied to **production DB** when GitHub syncs |
| `supabase/functions/` + `config.toml` | Edge functions deploy to **production** |
| `src/` frontend | **Not** live until **Publish → Update** in Lovable |

- New `[functions.*]` block in `supabase/config.toml` for every new edge function (same PR).
- New columns queried before `types.ts` regenerates: use `as unknown as YourRow[]` (see deployment guide).
- Destructive migrations: order-of-operations per the guide (code ↔ schema).

## Observability secrets (Lovable)

Before every push that touches frontend observability or edge logging/Sentry wiring, verify in Lovable secrets:

- Frontend build env (Lovable Cloud): `VITE_SENTRY_DSN`, `VITE_POSTHOG_KEY`, `VITE_POSTHOG_HOST`, `VITE_APP_VERSION` (= Git SHA).
- Edge secrets: `SENTRY_DSN_EDGES`, `SENTRY_RELEASE` (= same Git SHA), `SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT`, `LOG_DRAIN_URL`, `LOG_DRAIN_TOKEN`, `SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL`.
- CI build (source-map upload): `SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN`, `SENTRY_ORG`, `SENTRY_PROJECT` (optional — plugin no-ops without them).

Additional reminders:

- PostHog events added/renamed → also update [docs/ops/event-taxonomy.md](../../docs/ops/event-taxonomy.md) in the same PR.
- Feature flags added → also update [docs/ops/feature-flags.md](../../docs/ops/feature-flags.md) with owner, default, sunset trigger.
- `x-cid` propagation should remain intact — use the `invokeEdge` wrapper (or pass `withCidHeaders()`) on new edge call sites.
- New edge functions automatically inherit Sentry error capture via `withRequestLogging` + `_shared/observe.ts`; no per-function Sentry init required.
- New cron jobs need a corresponding BetterStack heartbeat UUID and an entry in [docs/ops/observability-setup.md](../../docs/ops/observability-setup.md) §6.

If the user asks only to "push" or "ship," still verify the checklist or state what was skipped and why.
